# No end-of-line conversion, on anything.
#
# This tree is mixed, but not by the map it used to carry. The comment below described
# the pre-export working tree and is fiction here:
#
#     Cargo.toml, CLAUDE.md, PERF.md and README.md are CRLF, while every .wgsl is LF and
#     .rs and docs/ are LF with exactly three exceptions -- src/lib.rs, src/stats.rs and
#     docs/batch-11-godrays.md ...
#
# A post-export census found none of that holds: the export pipeline normalised most of
# the tree to CRLF (117 files, including most of src/ and tests/ and all four names above),
# while 53 arrived LF (src/menu.rs, src/settings.rs, Cargo.lock and the newer .md docs),
# and docs/batch-11-godrays.md does not exist anywhere in this repository.
# Batch 22's "re-verified, still three" claim could not have been run against this tree.
# Do not trust any per-file ending claim -- including this one, if files are added after
# the census -- check the file before anchoring an edit on a newline.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which would normalise the LF files to
# CRLF in the working copy on the next checkout and quietly rewrite much of the source
# tree. `-text` turns that off so the bytes in a clone are the bytes that were committed.
# Diffs are unaffected.
* -text
